In an operation on a double held in registers (as a function returns one)
and a constant, such as 0.5 * exp(x), the constant was pushed first, a
word at a time through AX, which held the low word of the other operand:
the result came out with that word lost. The register operand is now
pushed first.

--- a/bcc/floatop.c
+++ b/bcc/floatop.c
@@ -104,6 +104,12 @@
 
     regmark = reguse;
     saveopreg();
+    /* A double still in registers (a function's result) goes on the stack
+     * before a constant is pushed: each word of a constant is pushed
+     * through AX, one of the registers it is in. */
+    if (target->indcount == 0 && target->storage != CONSTANT &&
+	source->indcount == 0 && source->storage == CONSTANT)
+	(void) f_indirect(target);
     (void) f_indirect(source);
     if (!(reguse & OPREG) && (source->storage == OPREG))
     {
